{:value "353548"} "Canadian Doubles, Slalom, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "353600"} "Kayak Singles, Slalom, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "255414"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "256033"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "256163"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "256278"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "256395"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258824"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "307000"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "19006320"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008406"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/174"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Canadian Singles, Slalom, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "7 –  9 August 2016"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/904"} "Estádio de Canoagem Slalom, Parque Olímpico de Deodoro, Deodoro, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/353542"} "19 from 19 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Slovakian " [:a {:href "/athletes/10719"} "Michal Martikán"] " and Frenchman " [:a {:href "/athletes/90175"} "Tony Estanguet"] " had dominated the Men’s C-1 Slalom since 1996 and, although they were not present in Rio, their compatriots " [:a {:href "/athletes/135976"} "Matej Beňuš"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/133830"} "Denis Gargaud Chanut"] " were positioned to continue their nations’ strong presence in the event. Beňuš had won 13 gold medals at the European and World Championships in the C-1 team, was the 2011 C-1 World bronze medallist, and had earned silver in the C-1 at the 2010 Europeans and bronze in the 2013 and 2015 editions. Chanut was less decorated, but among his C-1 honors were gold at the 2011 World Championships and bronze at the 2011 Europeans. " [:a {:href "/athletes/116471"} "David Florence"] " of Great Britain was also a strong contender, having been the 2013 and 2015 World Champion, as well as a silver medallist at the 2008 Summer Games, while Slovenia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/125768"} "Benjamin Savšek"] " was the 2015 European champion, a European bronze medallist in 2012, a World runner-up in 2014 and 2015, and World bronze medallist in 2013."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/125329"} "Sideris Tasiadis"] ", the 2012 European Champion and 2013 and 2015 European runner-up, came out ahead in the preliminary rounds, 1.25 ahead of Chanut and 1.88 ahead of Florence, and was still in front after the semi-finals. In the final, however, Chanut came back to win the gold medal, while Beňuš, who had finished sixth and eighth in the preliminaries and semi-final respectively, made an impressive run that eventually earned him silver. Savšek and Florence both suffered from major penalties, however, and even Tasiadis took a costly two-second hit that paved the way for Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/116477"} "Takuya Haneda"] " to win bronze, which was Asia’s first Olympic medal in canoeing. Another notable entrant was Lebanon’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/135027"} "Richard Merjan"] " who, despite finishing last, earned distinction as his country’s first Olympic canoeist."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133830"} "Denis Gargaud Chanut"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-al